**Closing — already fixed on `main`.** Two actions in one comment, both by the `repo:objectui` PM seat, round 6, session `session_01RV6yuVCxymHYE16PL9vQkE`.

## 1. Assignee removed (the stale-claim window expired)

The probe on this card was posted **2026-08-18 14:23Z** and asked the holder of `os-zhuang` to say so if the work was live. At the time of this comment that is **5.5 hours** of silence, on top of the twelve days the assignment had already stood. Against the evidence readable from GitHub — no claim comment (the only `os-zhuang` comment here is explicitly labelled *「本评论来自分诊座位 Routine…不构成认领」*), no branch, no PR — the claim is stale and the assignee is removed.

**Provenance for the unassign**: acting on the seat's own probe protocol, per the reclaim criteria stated in that probe comment. It was not reassigned to me by that act, exactly as the probe promised.

## 2. The card is already delivered — verified on `origin/main`

I ran the premise check before dispatching, because triage's own comment warned that this card was filed 2026-08-01 and *「派发前在当前 main 上重跑三步复现」*. That warning earned its keep: **the fix is on `main`.**

`packages/app-shell/src/views/studio-design/ObjectFormDesigner.tsx` now resolves both label channels through the hook the card said was being bypassed:

```
const { fieldLabel, sectionLabel } = useSafeFieldLabel();

const fieldLabelOf = React.useCallback((entry: FieldEntry) => {
  const fallback = String(entry.def.label ?? entry.name);
  return objectName ? fieldLabel(objectName, entry.name, fallback) : fallback;
}, [objectName, fieldLabel]);

// …and for group titles:
const fallback = g.label || g.key;
m.set(cid(g.key), objectName ? sectionLabel(objectName, g.key, fallback) : fallback);
```

`entry.def.label` and `g.label` still appear — which is exactly why a grep alone would have been misleading — but they are now the **fallback arguments** to `fieldLabel` / `sectionLabel`, not the displayed values. That is the wiring the card asked for.

It also carries a named regression test, `ObjectFormDesigner.test.tsx`:

```
describe('ObjectFormDesigner — object translations (objectui#3134)', …)
```

whose header states the defect in the past tense — *"It **used to** read `entry.def.label` and `group.label` straight off the draft metadata, so a fully translated object still rendered its English source labels in the designer"* — and pins the `crm_opportunity` / `Opportunity Name` / `Basic Information` case this card reported, against a `zh` instance.

The choice of `useSafeFieldLabel` (the provider-safe wrapper) over `useObjectLabel` directly is deliberate and documented in the source: the designer is also mounted in tests and previews with no `I18nProvider`, where it degrades to an identity fallback.

Closing as **completed**. Whoever landed it did so without closing this card — the fix is real and pinned, so the card is finished regardless of which PR carried it.

## Note for the seat, recorded because it nearly cost a dispatch

This is the **third** card today that was already fixed before I looked at it, and the first one I caught **before** spending a dev on it. The difference was mechanical, not attentiveness: triage had written "re-run the repro on current main before dispatching" into the card, and I ran it. #5217 had no such line and I dispatched it into an empty problem.

**The generalisation: a card's age is itself a premise-check trigger.** This one was 17 days old; the fix landed somewhere in that window without closing it. Cards do not announce that they have gone stale — the only defence is measuring at dispatch time, every time.

